<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://aminizahra.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://aminizahra.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-02T16:41:10+00:00</updated><id>https://aminizahra.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>A simple, whitespace theme for academics. Based on [*folio](https://github.com/bogoli/-folio) design. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Python for AI, Step 1: Variables and Data Types</title><link href="https://aminizahra.github.io/blog/2026/python-step-1-variables/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Python for AI, Step 1: Variables and Data Types"/><published>2026-10-02T10:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-10-02T10:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://aminizahra.github.io/blog/2026/python-step-1-variables</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://aminizahra.github.io/blog/2026/python-step-1-variables/"><![CDATA[<p>This is the first step of the Python series. By the end you will know how to store information in variables and which basic data types Python gives you.</p> <h4 id="what-you-will-learn">What you will learn</h4> <ul> <li>What a variable is and how to name one</li> <li>The four basic data types: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">int</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">float</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">str</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">bool</code></li> <li>How to check a type and convert between types</li> </ul> <h4 id="variables">Variables</h4> <p>A variable is a name that points to a value.</p> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">age</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="mi">25</span>
<span class="n">height</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="mf">1.68</span>
<span class="n">name</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">Zahra</span><span class="sh">"</span>
<span class="n">is_student</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="bp">True</span>

<span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">name</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">age</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <h4 id="basic-data-types">Basic data types</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Type</th> <th>Example</th> <th>Use</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">int</code></td> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">25</code></td> <td>whole numbers</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">float</code></td> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">1.68</code></td> <td>decimal numbers</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">str</code></td> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"Zahra"</code></td> <td>text</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">bool</code></td> <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">True</code></td> <td>yes or no</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Check the type of any value with <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">type()</code>:</p> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">type</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">age</span><span class="p">))</span>      <span class="c1"># &lt;class 'int'&gt;
</span><span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">type</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">height</span><span class="p">))</span>   <span class="c1"># &lt;class 'float'&gt;
</span></code></pre></div></div> <h4 id="converting-types">Converting types</h4> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">price</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">120</span><span class="sh">"</span>
<span class="n">total</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">int</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">price</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="mi">3</span>
<span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">total</span><span class="p">)</span>   <span class="c1"># 360
</span></code></pre></div></div> <h4 id="practice">Practice</h4> <ol> <li>Create variables for your name, your age and your favourite number.</li> <li>Print a sentence that uses all three.</li> <li>Convert the string <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"3.14"</code> to a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">float</code> and multiply it by 2.</li> </ol> <hr/> <p><strong>Next step:</strong> Conditions (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">if</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">elif</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">else</code>).</p> <p>Code and notebooks for this series: <a href="https://github.com/hobotacademy/Python-for-AI">Python-for-AI on GitHub</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="python"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Store values, understand the basic data types, and run your first Python code.]]></summary></entry></feed>